(INVOICE FINANCING AGREEMENT) Tj T*
T*
(Agreement No. GBR-IF-2026-118) Tj T*
T*
(Synthetic demonstration document, written to match the TermsLedger demo scenario. It is not a real) Tj T*
(agreement and binds no one.) Tj T*
T*
(This Agreement is made on 28 August 2026 between Greater Bay Receivables Finance Co., Ltd. \(the) Tj T*
("Financier"\) and Lingnan Homeware Manufacturing Co., Ltd. \(the "Client"\).) Tj T*
T*
(1. THE FACILITY) Tj T*
T*
(1.1 The Financier provides the Client with an invoice financing facility with a facility limit of RMB 350,000.) Tj T*
T*
(1.2 Advance rate: the Financier advances 80% of the face amount of each eligible invoice.) Tj T*
T*
(1.3 An invoice is eligible if it is issued to a buyer approved by the Financier, confirmed by that buyer and not) Tj T*
(overdue.) Tj T*
T*
(2. DISBURSEMENT) Tj T*
T*
(2.1 Each advance is disbursed within three \(3\) days of an accepted financing request.) Tj T*
T*
(3. CHARGES) Tj T*
T*
(3.1 Interest: the interest rate is 7.8% per annum on the amount advanced.) Tj T*
T*
(3.2 Service fee: a service fee of 0.25% of each advance is charged for each period of thirty \(30\) days, or part) Tj T*
(of such a period, for which the advance is outstanding.) Tj T*
T*
(4. REPAYMENT) Tj T*
T*
(4.1 Each advance is repaid from the buyer's payment of the financed invoice, which the Client shall direct to) Tj T*
(the collection account of the Financier.) Tj T*
T*
(5. SECURITY) Tj T*
T*
(5.1 No personal guarantee, collateral or pledge is required under this Agreement.) Tj T*
T*
(6. GOVERNING LAW) Tj T*
T*
(6.1 This Agreement is governed by the laws of the People's Republic of China.) Tj T*
T*
(Signed for the Financier: Huang Jie, Head of Client Finance. Date: 28 August 2026.) Tj T*
T*
(Signed for the Client: Chen Wei, Director. Date: 28 August 2026.) Tj T*
